<header class="hero" id="top">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="hero-grid">
      <div>
        <h1>What would it take to trust our migration system?</h1>
        <p class="sub">In October 2026, Kate Chaney MP and RadicalxChange asked Curtin. <b>266 people</b> took part, casting <b>21,433 votes</b> to agree or disagree with <b>537 statements</b>.</p>
        <div class="actions"><a class="btn solid" href="#groups">See what Curtin said</a><a class="btn line" href="https://pol.is/report/r9fyrr8m6yfmfbwscfvp2">Explore the full data</a></div>
      </div>
      <div class="cards" role="list" aria-label="Four statements from the conversation">
        <div class="card c1" role="listitem"><q>Immigration is fundamentally a good thing. But, for all concerned the rules should be clear. Decisions should be made promptly.</q></div>
        <div class="card c2" role="listitem"><q>Employers who exploit migrant workers should lose the right to sponsor visas.</q></div>
        <div class="card c3" role="listitem"><q>Migration keeps my workplace and my community going. Cutting it back would cost us more than it would save.</q></div>
        <div class="card c4" role="listitem"><q>For me, trust comes down to the numbers: too many people have arrived too quickly for our communities to keep up.</q></div>
        <div class="sticker" aria-hidden="true"><div><b>501</b><span>statements written<br>by the community</span></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<main>
<section class="glance" aria-label="At a glance">
  <div class="wrap glance-grid">
    <a class="gl" href="#groups">
      <h3>Curtin splits in two</h3>
      <div class="split84" aria-hidden="true"><i style="width:16%;background:var(--g1)"></i><i style="width:84%;background:var(--g2)"></i></div>
      <div class="split84-n" aria-hidden="true"><span><i class="dot g1"></i>16%</span><span>84%<i class="dot g2"></i></span></div>
      <p>Of the 233 people placed in a group, 84% see migration working. 16% want fewer people, arriving more slowly.</p>
      <span class="more">See the groups</span>
    </a>
    <a class="gl dark" href="#agree">
      <h3>Even where they disagree, they agree on something</h3>
      <p>On the topics that divide them most, both groups back seasonal visas, infrastructure that keeps pace, and respect for Australian laws and values.</p>
      <span class="more">See where they agree</span>
    </a>
    <a class="gl tinted" href="#priorities">
      <h3>Top priority: a 10-year plan</h3>
      <p>65 of 73 voters backed a ten-year migration plan reported to Parliament. Five of the top six priorities echo ideas most people in both groups supported.</p>
      <span class="more">See the priorities</span>
    </a>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="block" id="groups" aria-labelledby="groups-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head">
      <h2 id="groups-h">Curtin splits into two groups</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="groups-row">
      <div class="gcard one">
        <div class="gtop"><span class="big">16<span class="pc">%</span></span><span class="who"><b>Group 1: Pace and control</b>37 people</span></div>
        <div class="qbox lead"><p class="lab">What sets them apart most</p><q>A temporary visa should not lead to permanent residency.</q>
          <div class="pcts"><span><i class="dot g1"></i><b>94%</b> of Group 1 agree <span class="nn">(17 voted)</span></span><span><i class="dot g2"></i><b>16%</b> of Group 2</span></div></div>
        <div class="qbox"><q>For me, trust comes down to the numbers: too many people have arrived too quickly for our communities to keep up.</q>
          <div class="pcts"><span><i class="dot g1"></i><b>89%</b> of Group 1 agree</span><span><i class="dot g2"></i><b>25%</b> of Group 2</span></div></div>
        <div class="qbox"><q>We need net negative migration to ease housing and raise wages. Big business is funding mass migration and selling out Aussies</q>
          <div class="pcts"><span><i class="dot g1"></i><b>80%</b> of Group 1 agree <span class="nn">(15 voted)</span></span><span><i class="dot g2"></i><b>2%</b> of Group 2</span></div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="gcard two">
        <div class="gtop"><span class="big">84<span class="pc">%</span></span><span class="who"><b>Group 2: Migration works</b>196 people</span></div>
        <div class="qbox lead"><p class="lab">What sets them apart most</p><q>Migration keeps my workplace and my community going. Cutting it back would cost us more than it would save.</q>
          <div class="pcts"><span><i class="dot g2"></i><b>82%</b> of Group 2 agree</span><span><i class="dot g1"></i><b>7%</b> of Group 1</span></div></div>
        <div class="qbox"><q>Australians should not forget we are all migrants except for First Nations people as so deal with newer migrants humanely</q>
          <div class="pcts"><span><i class="dot g2"></i><b>92%</b> of Group 2 agree</span><span><i class="dot g1"></i><b>14%</b> of Group 1 <span class="nn">(14 voted)</span></span></div></div>
        <div class="qbox"><q>Someone who has lived, worked and paid tax here for years, and whose kids grew up here, deserves a real path to stay.</q>
          <div class="pcts"><span><i class="dot g2"></i><b>96%</b> of Group 2 agree</span><span><i class="dot g1"></i><b>47%</b> of Group 1</span></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="small-note">Group 1 is likely smaller here than in Curtin as a whole, because the people who join a conversation like this aren’t a random sample. 33 people voted on too few statements to be placed in a group.</p>

    <div class="sub-head"><h3>Where everyone sits</h3></div>
    <div class="map-card" id="map-card">
      <p class="map-lead">Each dot is one person. People who voted alike sit close together.</p>
      <div class="map-top">
        <div class="map-legend"><span><i class="dot g1"></i>Group 1: Pace and control</span><span><i class="dot g2"></i>Group 2: Migration works</span><span style="font-weight:400"><i class="dot pale"></i>Paler: voted partly like the other group</span></div>
        <button class="someone" type="button" id="someone">Show me someone</button>
      </div>
      <svg id="map" viewBox="0 0 1000 560" role="img" aria-labelledby="map-desc"><desc id="map-desc">A map of 233 people. Group 1, 37 people, sits on the left, where people agreed that fewer migrants should arrive more slowly. Group 2, 196 people, sits on the right, where people agreed that migration is working. Higher up are people who agreed with more statements overall.</desc></svg>
      <div class="person" id="person" aria-live="polite"></div>
      <p class="map-hint">Hover over or tap a dot to see how that person voted.</p>
    </div>


  </div>
</section>

<section class="block deep" id="agree" aria-labelledby="agree-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head">
      <h2 id="agree-h">Even where they disagree, they agree on something</h2>
    </div>
    <div id="pairs"></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="block" id="open" aria-labelledby="open-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head">
      <h2 id="open-h">Some questions split both groups the same way</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="open-grid" id="open-grid"></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="block tint" id="priorities" aria-labelledby="prio-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head">
      <h2 id="prio-h">The six changes people want most</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="how">
      <div class="costs" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="cost"><div class="sq s1"><i></i></div><p><b>1 vote</b><br>1 credit</p></div>
        <div class="cost"><div class="sq s4"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><p><b>2 votes</b><br>4 credits</p></div>
        <div class="cost"><div class="sq s9"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><p><b>3 votes</b><br>9 credits</p></div>
      </div>
      <p class="cap">On 14 October, 73 people used quadratic voting to spread a budget of credits across 13 possible changes, for or against. Each extra vote on the same idea costs more, so the totals show what people care about most.</p>
    </div>
    <p class="finding">Five of the top six echo ideas that most people in both groups backed in the conversation.</p>
    <div class="key" aria-hidden="true"><span><i style="background:var(--fizz);box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1.5px rgba(0,0,0,.6)"></i>Backed it</span><span><i style="background:var(--ink)"></i>Opposed it</span><span><i style="background:var(--track)"></i>Neither</span></div>
    <div class="prio-grid" id="prio"></div>
    <div class="no-card">
      <div><h3>And one clear no</h3><p class="t">Prioritise migrants in high-paying jobs, using salary rather than shortage lists to decide who qualifies.</p><p class="s">44 people opposed it and 13 backed it. Most of the opposition was mild, with one or two votes each.</p></div>
      <div><div class="waffle" id="nowaffle" role="img" aria-label="13 of 73 backed it, 44 opposed it"></div><div class="pstats" style="color:#fff"><span><b>13</b> backed, <b>44</b> opposed</span><span>Net <b>−75</b> votes</span></div></div>
    </div>
    <details class="rest">
      <summary>See the other six changes</summary>
      <ol class="rest-list" id="rest"></ol>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="block" id="about" aria-labelledby="about-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head"><h2 id="about-h">How this worked</h2></div>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li class="step"><span class="fig">36</span><h3>Starter statements</h3><p>Kate Chaney’s team and RadicalxChange wrote the first statements to open the conversation.</p></li>
      <li class="step"><span class="fig">266</span><h3>People took part</h3><p>From 8 to 27 October they voted agree, disagree or pass, online or at a workshop on 14 October, and added 501 statements of their own.</p></li>
      <li class="step"><span class="fig">2</span><h3>Groups emerged</h3><p>Polis, an open-source tool, grouped people who voted alike. Nobody chose a group. We named them.</p></li>
      <li class="step"><span class="fig">73</span><h3>Voters set priorities</h3><p>On 14 October they spread a budget of credits across 13 possible changes, using quadratic voting.</p></li>
    </ol>
    <details class="fine">
      <summary>Notes for checking the numbers</summary>
      <div class="arows">
        <div class="arow"><h3>Reading the percentages</h3><p>Each figure is the share of a group who agreed, out of those in the group who voted on that statement. Later statements had fewer voters, so where fewer than 20 people in a group voted, we show how many.</p></div>
        <div class="arow"><h3>Reading the map</h3><p>We rebuilt the map from the published votes using the same method as Polis, so it is close to the Polis report but not identical. Left to right is the main divide. Up and down is how often people agreed overall. The 32 paler dots are people near the border who voted partly like the other group, mostly people who voted on fewer statements.</p></div>
        <div class="arow"><h3>Pairing the statements</h3><p>RadicalxChange chose which statements to pair. Every number comes straight from the results. People who took part online and at the 14 October workshop gave very similar results.</p></div>
        <div class="arow"><h3>The priority vote</h3><p>A separate vote with its own voters. We set aside ballots that used fewer than 10 credits and kept the fuller ballot where someone voted twice, leaving 73 voters. Net votes are votes for minus votes against. The matching statements from the conversation are close in meaning, not identical in wording.</p></div>
        <div class="arow"><h3>The data</h3><p>From the Polis export of 30 October 2026, after voting closed on 27 October. Statements appear exactly as people wrote them.</p></div>
      </div>
    </details>
    <div class="links"><a class="btn solid" href="https://pol.is/report/r9fyrr8m6yfmfbwscfvp2">Full Polis report</a><a class="btn line" href="https://pol.is/2mjb35sdvd">The Polis conversation</a></div>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="next" aria-labelledby="next-h">
  <div class="wrap next-grid">
    <div>
      <h2 id="next-h">What happens next</h2>
      <p>Kate Chaney and her team will be working with these results. More soon, so stay tuned!</p>
      <div class="actions"><a class="btn solid" href="https://pol.is/report/r9fyrr8m6yfmfbwscfvp2">Explore the full data</a><a class="btn line" href="#top">Back to the top</a></div>
    </div>
    <div class="sticker2" aria-hidden="true"><div><b>Thank you, Curtin</b></div></div>
  </div>
</section>
