quickly for our communities to keep up.","131":"If there is a housing shortage, is immigration fuelling an increase in house prices and so the affordability crisi we hear about?","134":"Migration has worked well and should be seen as a positive","8":"Migration keeps my workplace and my community going. Cutting it back would cost us more than it would save.","392":"Shelter is a basic human right, and if our kids cannot buy/rent their own homes, the immigration numbers need to be reduced drastically","144":"Migrants have enhanced our culture and economy.","22":"Migration is about people, not just workers. Families being able to live together should count as much as economic contribution.","27":"If we expect newcomers to learn English, classes and settlement support should be funded for everyone, not just permanent arrivals.","31":"The culture of my community is changing faster than people can adjust, and it’s fair to worry about that.","34":"As a lucky country, we have a duty to keep helping people who aren’t so lucky, even when it costs us.","165":"Migrant crime is a real issue and threatening to our way of life","294":"the government needs to be extracting money from large multinational corporations not migrants and international students","168":"We need net negative migration to ease housing and raise wages. Big business is funding mass migration and selling out Aussies","171":"Mass migration is destroying social cohesion, we need a 5 year pause on all migration","172":"New migrants who come to a prosperous nation are not the same as the brave settlers who built the country from nothing but dirt","176":"Australians should not forget we are all migrants except for First Nations people as so deal with newer migrants humanely","178":"All too often migrants are blamed for the difficulties people experience during challenging times.","61":"International students add to the quality of Australian education by bringing different perspectives.","66":"People would support our migration system more if it was acknowledged that there are some countries which we should not take migrants from","69":"A temporary visa should not lead to permanent residency.","198":"Social benefits should only apply to citizens.","86":"Why can’t family reunions can take place in the country of origin, why should the Australian taxpayer fund someone’s family to come here?","215":"International students contribute to our economy and society and should be treated as guests, not a burden.","346":"The housing crisis is a direct result of large volumes of migration","95":"Migrants are not the problem with the housing market","96":"Migrants bring valued traditions to our communities","224":"Migrants on visas should have access to services like medicare","98":"Helping families reunite is an important part of a working migration shstem","103":"Without migration the economic burden to provide for an ageing population will fall to fewer people.","109":"The process for family migration, in particular for older parents joining their Australian citizen children needs to be quicker and clearer","113":"Anti migration sentiment is unfortunately always targeted at black / brown skin tones.","249":"When bringing in people from trouble spots, we need to fund extra support to help them settle.","122":"I don’t have a problem with genuine refugees provided they are vetted but I do have a problem with assylum seekers being given a free run.","123":"The migration debate seems to have become more racist and less trusted since cost-of-living became a real issue here."},"nsplit":40};
